<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lake George</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1755</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lake George was fought on 8 September 1755 at the southern end of Lake George in the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, early in the French and Indian War. British colonial troops under William Johnson and Mohawk warriors under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hendrick-theyanoguin">Hendrick Theyanoguin</a>, who was killed, repulsed an attack by French regulars, Canadians and allied Native warriors under Baron Dieskau, who was captured. The British then built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-william-henry">Fort William Henry</a> on the site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lake-george.jpg" alt="Battle of Lake George" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin West · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johnson_saving_Dieskau.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
